  "inclusion_rules": [
    {
      "id": "ran_to_cap",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 1: it ran to its decode cap, or was cut by T_dead where the design says it should be. No leg in this kit has a designed cut. A type-A leg's cap is 4,096; a type-L leg's cap is its own (3,724, 3,151 or 4,096; RL-150 section 3.2), recorded on the leg as decode_tokens and in its result as decode_cap. A leg that stops short of its own cap is kept in custody, flagged, and not included."
    },
    {
      "id": "g0_released",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 2: its G0 released, under the R1 G0 timeout of 1,200 s, against the reference its kit shape names: its own capture (g0_shape own, and the first leg of each span), or the span's reference, the authenticated capture of the span's first leg (g0_shape span, RL-150 R1 part 2). A leg whose G0 timed out runs no turn, stays in custody and is not included."
    },
    {
      "id": "sidecar_coverage",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 3: sidecar coverage of at least 99 % with no gap over 2 s, and powermetrics gaps within the U1 bound. Judged on custody by frozen code at a look, not by the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "km003c_clean",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 4: the KM003C was present and its stream is clean, since every leg is analysed on DC-in as well as the GPU rail."
    },
    {
      "id": "not_a_replaced_attempt",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 5 as amended by RL-150 R7: it is not an attempt judged contaminated under the load-redo rule (above 0.5 core of outside load for 60 s), whether or not a redo replaced it. The runner redoes such a leg once per contaminated attempt, up to the span's redo quota; every replaced attempt stays in custody as runtime.rejected<N>."
    },
    {
      "id": "block_power_mode",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.4 rule 6: the power mode is the block's. This block is Automatic (pmset powermode 0)."
    },
    {
      "id": "no_drop_by_outcome",
      "text": "No leg is dropped for its energy, its residual, its OS level or state, or its heat. Those are the measurement. Every attempt stays in custody, replaced ones included."
    },
    {
      "id": "bands_by_history",
      "text": "RL-149 section 2.2 and RL-181 section 3.3: q0 begins at the leg's G0 release. The first A follows the fresh soak and supplies the span reference; the other five consume it. The pinned qualification law draws the A order and adjacent L-pair placement."
    },
    {
      "id": "reserve_rule",
      "text": "RL-181 section 3.1: transfer uses its own 120-leg ceiling. No transfer leg is replaced. A missed opportunity spends its place and never uses the twelve-leg reserve."
    },
    {
      "id": "energy_read_rule",
      "text": "RL-179 F-12, RL-180 and RL-181 section 3.6: frozen code reads the committed roster only at lm-transfer-01 after the terminal calendar and desks close. The desk uses only operational projections. The kit has no executable look hook."
    }
  ],
  "stop_rules": {
    "instrument_fault": true,
    "refusal": true,
    "contaminated_redos_max": 3,
    "contaminated_redos_scope": "span",
    "band_unreachable_max": 2,
    "band_unreachable_scope": "span",
    "leg_time_factor": 1.5,
    "notes": "RL-179 F-6 and F-9: Watcher loss raises an alarm only. A changed frozen path removes only that entry from admission. An unplanned restart has no admission effect. Keep hygiene settings fixed from freeze 2 through qual-03 close. Unproven restore or an unowned High Power marker stops all work. Retry the pinned restore once and verify the readback, then halt and page if it fails. Disk below the floor stops all work until the disk check passes. Meter absent or not polling, or collector startup failure, stops measured work until the launcher's instrument check passes. Tell the research lead. CONTAMINATED_REDOS at three in a span holds counted and v4 entries until a later span on the host closes with neither a load redo nor a load flag. A filler may probe. Apply the counted batch hold under RL-180 row 8. LEG_OVERTIME, a non-clean close, launcher refusal, desk failure or a failed consumer gate holds the affected kit or block until an input changes. Refer a consumer failure to the research lead under RL-179 F-3. The pinned runner models leg budgets and process caps."
  },
